N:2. 'Twas grace that taught my heart to fear
N:And grace that fear relieved;
N:How precious did that grace appear
N:The hour I first believed.
N:3. Through many dangers, toils, and snares
N:I have already come;
N:'Tis grace hath bro't me safe thus far,
N:And grace will lead me home.
N:4. When we've been here ten thousand years
N:Bright shining as the sun;
N:We've no less days to sing God's praise
N:Than when we first begun.
